# Badly Drawn Why videos

When the user wants a video, a next episode, or paint/storyboard work, finish the package. Do not wait to be asked separately for frames, voice, title, description, or thumbnail.

The user only uploads: the MP4, the thumbnail, and the Studio text.

Active brand must be `badly-drawn-why`. «yeni video» means **one** episode from the next unshipped topic in `scenarios/topics-paint.json` (skip `guidance` that starts with `SHIPPED`). Then stop.

## Always do

1. Research from named sources. Do not invent quotes or dates. Humor at systems/objects, never at people, groups, or the injured. No gore, crash closeups, flags as the joke, medical advice.
2. Write the English spoken essay yourself (11 minutes unless they say otherwise). Do not ship a thin Ollama draft. Cold open in "you", open loop, named facts, rehook, modern "this is you", callback. No "welcome back" / "in this video". Cars and historical objects/systems are in-niche as why essays. Not a Drawn Anyway event recap.
3. Invent timestamps and unique visual beats at one still every 5 seconds of the target runtime (about 132 for 11 minutes).
4. Draw 16:9 MS Paint stickman stills (ChatGPT Image 2) plus one yellow-hook thumbnail. Save under `output/storyboard/<project_id>/` as `NN-slug.png` and `thumbnail.png`.
5. Build a `paint` scenario and run `python main.py run --scenario senaryo-paint.json --no-upload`.
6. Hand over `output/final/*.mp4`, `output/thumbnails/*.jpg`, `output/studio/*/STUDIO.txt`. Mark the topic `SHIPPED YYYYMMDD`. Do not chain to the next topic.

## Never

- YouTube API upload
- Pexels on paint videos
- Asking the user to draw, narrate, or write title/description/thumbnail
- Ink mascot, candy cartoon, or `senaryo-drawn.json` on this brand
